menuconfig MODULES_FLIP_RIG_AXIS
	bool "flip_rig_axis"
	default n
	---help---
		Enable support for flip_rig_axis

		Standalone, manually-started single-shot 360 degree flip
		controller for a fixture that physically prevents translation
		(e.g. a 3-axis gimbal/gyroscope test rig), driven through the
		ATTITUDE setpoint path (mc_att_control) instead of raw body
		rates. Generalises flip_rig_pitch_att: the rotation axis is a
		free parameter anywhere in the body xy-plane (FRIGAX_AXIS), so
		the same module performs roll flips, pitch flips, and any
		diagonal in between. Never touches position/GPS - start with
		`flip_rig_axis start` and do not run it alongside another
		OFFBOARD-publishing module. The instant OFFBOARD is engaged it
		latches the vehicle's current yaw, executes exactly one 360
		degree rotation about the chosen axis by chasing a
		continuously-advancing attitude setpoint, then commands a level
		attitude at the latched yaw and holds it.
